ons  yesterday glasgow is the only area in  scotland so far accepting asylum seekers  in the uk's government scheme  well we are also as i just said  welcoming  refugees from afghanistan all local  authorities really stepped up when it  came to  ensuring that syrian refugees could be  resettled at glasgow is right now a key  location when it comes to asylum seekers  but right now obviously it is a uk  government power but where we can play  our role scotland is the scottish  government is ensuring that there is  housing available that there is health  care provision made for those refugees  that are fleeing i think the bottom line  for me though is that we are seeing  reports on the front pages of newspapers  of mothers and babies drowning in the  channel because the system is not  working and we only see a few stories  that make it onto the newspapers  most of them don't so something  drastically needs to change  we don't have long so i'm just going to  cut in there if that's all right you're  right it is dreadful those scenes that  we're seeing on the front page of  newspapers are absolutely horrifying so  let's cut through the politics we need  cross-party solutions on this what would  you propose  so we do need cross-party solutions so  firstly i think that european leaders  need to get together to determine how  they are going to ensure safe passage  for those refugees and asylum seekers  that need it the most secondly we need  to see the uk take more refugees and  asylum seekers we know already that  germany and france  are taking it more refugees and that's  the second thing thirdly when refugees  and asylum seekers arrive they need to  be treated humanely we know about the  backlogs when it comes to the home  office we know that there is a hostile  environment that is an intentional  policy decision that needs to change  these are human beings so there's three  suggestions to start with  so obviously a bus ride a nine hour bus  ride as it's been described to