r members to be involved in  a situation  where people have weapons and our staff  do not  now the other big political story this  morning is this new uh temporary travel  ban that's been brought in  against six countries in southern africa  as someone who's had to  work on uk borders in the last couple of  years during the pandemic  in your experience  uh how much chaos and confusion does  this sort of measure throw up  it depends on the amount of checking  that waterfalls are being asked to do  and at the moment they've not actually  been asked to do any and so we won't get  flights direct from those countries uh  individuals who've flown from those  countries via a connecting flight will  simply come through in in the normal way  unless they do something to attract the  attention of a border officer for  another reason they're not likely to be  identified uh it's not clear yet um  whether there's going to be any extended  checking to ensure that individuals have  not arrived via a third country if that  is brought in if border force are  required again to extend the amount of  checks that they need to do for arriving  passengers at uh warts and seaports then  that will inevitably slow up uh the  process of people through the border and  it will result in an increased level of  queues but my understanding right at the  moment is that border force have not  been asked to take any part in ensuring  that individuals have not transited a  third country  and just very briefly before i let you  go of course there's a lot of finger  pointing between france and the uk about  what needs to be done about the  situation in the channel as someone who  actually has to work on the front line  of the uk border what would be the one  thing that you would want to see change  if something could be changed right now  it seems to us that the only thing that  the uk can control is itself  and so the only thing that that we can  really ask for is that the processes and  systems and resources within the uk are  adequately resourced for this so in  order to get people off the floor of tug  haven we need to be able to get them out  the other side of the process into local  authority housing those local  authorities need the funding to be able  to house folk we need resources to make  the asylum decisions resources into the  courts so that we can go through the  appeals process resources into  immigration enforcement so that once the  process is concluded uh we can arrest  these individuals and enforce their  removal if we have to if the only thing  the uk can do is control its own funding  and its own borders then let's resource  that properly  okay lucy morton we appreciate your  insight best of luck with your work  thank you very  much
 

